│ through an intravenous line at the beginning peritoneum suture. PONV by Index of Nausea Vomiting and Retching        │
│ (INVR), nausea by Visual Analogue Scale (VAS), and pain (VAS) were assessed at postoperative 1 hr, 3 hr, 6 hr, 24    │
│ hr, and 48 hr. Data were analyzed using repeated measures ANOVA, and Bonferroni methods. RESULTS The experimental    │
│ group that received ondansetron combined with dexamethasone had less PONV (p=.048), and nausea (p=.012) than control │
│ group that received ondansetron alone. However, there was no difference in pain (p=.557) between the patients in the │
│ two groups. CONCLUSION We conclude that the administration of ondansetron combined with dexamethasone is more        │
