  compared with midazolam (5–7.5 mg) used to supplement fentanyl-N2Cambridge University Press'}, {'study_index': 402,   
  'title': 'Effectiveness of antiemetic prophylaxis with methylprednisolone, granisetron and their combination on       
  postoperative nausea and vomiting following thyroid surgery', 'abstract': 'Materials and Methods: One hundred ninety  
  five (195) patients scheduled for elective thyroid and parathyroid surgery were randomly allocated (n= 65 in each     
  group) to receive 40 mg methylprednisolone iv one hour before induction and 8 hours after skin closure (group M),     
  granisetron 1mg iv at the end of surgery (group G) or combination of two drugs (group GM). Recruited patients were    
  adult, euthyroid, with predicted risk for PONV> 40% according to Apfel\'s score. They were operated under GA with     
