comprised morphine and atropine premedication and a halothane, nitrous oxide and oxygen spontaneous breathing technique.
No significant beneficial effects resulted from intra‐operative antiemetics; vomiting incidences of 26% after saline and
droperidol, 28% after metoclopramide and 14% after prochlorperazine were observed. Younger patients and females vomited 
